{"id":"mahabharata-3-031","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":31,"title":"एकत्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 31 · Draupadi questions providence","summary":{"en":"Draupadi laments that the Creator treats beings like wooden puppets, letting the righteous suffer while the wicked prosper. If karma does not reach the doer, she says, then only power matters, and she grieves for the weak.","kn":"ಸೃಷ್ಟಿಕರ್ತನು ಜೀವಿಗಳನ್ನು ಮರದ ಗೊಂಬೆಗಳಂತೆ ಆಡಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಧರ್ಮಿಷ್ಠರು ನರಳುತ್ತಾರೆ ದುಷ್ಟರು ಏಳಿಗೆ ಹೊಂದುತ್ತಾರೆ ಎಂದು ದ್ರೌಪದಿ ವಿಲಪಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಕರ್ಮಫಲ ಕರ್ತನನ್ನು ತಲುಪದಿದ್ದರೆ ಬಲವೊಂದೇ ಮುಖ್ಯ, ದುರ್ಬಲರಿಗಾಗಿ ತಾನು ಶೋಕಿಸುವೆ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"द्रौपदी विलाप करती हैं कि विधाता प्राणियों को काठ की कठपुतलियों की तरह नचाता है, धर्मात्मा दुःख पाते हैं और दुष्ट फलते-फूलते हैं। वे कहती हैं कि यदि कर्मफल कर्ता तक न पहुँचे तो केवल बल ही मायने रखता है, और वे दुर्बलों के लिए शोक करती हैं।","te":"సృష్టికర్త జీవులను చెక్కబొమ్మల్లా ఆడిస్తాడని, ధర్మాత్ములు కష్టపడుతుండగా దుర్మార్గులు వర్ధిల్లుతున్నారని ద్రౌపది విలపిస్తుంది. కర్మఫలం కర్తను చేరకపోతే బలమొక్కటే ముఖ్యమని, బలహీనుల కోసం తాను దుఃఖిస్తున్నానంటుంది.","ta":"படைப்பவன் உயிர்களை மரப்பொம்மைகளைப் போல் ஆட்டுவிக்கிறான், நல்லோர் துன்புற, தீயோர் செழிக்கிறார்கள் என்று திரௌபதி புலம்புகிறாள். வினைப்பயன் செய்தவனை அடையவில்லை என்றால் வலிமை ஒன்றே முக்கியம், பலவீனர்களுக்காகத் தான் வருந்துகிறேன் என்கிறாள்.","ml":"സൃഷ്ടികർത്താവ് ജീവികളെ മരപ്പാവകളെപ്പോലെ കളിപ്പിക്കുന്നുവെന്ന് ദ്രൗപദി വിലപിക്കുന്നു: നീതിമാൻ ദുരിതമനുഭവിക്കുകയും ദുഷ്ടൻ അഭിവൃദ്ധി നേടുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു. കർമ്മഫലം ചെയ്തവനിൽ എത്തുന്നില്ലെങ്കിൽ ശക്തി മാത്രമാണ് പ്രധാനം എന്നും, ദുർബലരെയോർത്ത് തനിക്ക് ദുഃഖമുണ്ടെന്നും അവൾ പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.31; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"कैरातपर्व","titleEn":"Kairata Parva (The mountain hunter)","verses":[{"text":"द्रौपद्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"नमो धात्रे विधात्रे च यौ मोहं चक्रतुस्तव ।\nपितृपैतामहे वृत्ते वोढव्ये तेऽन्यथा मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Homage to the Ordainer and the Disposer, who have deluded you; though you follow the conduct of your father and grandfather, your mind has gone another way.\""}},{"n":2,"text":"नेह धर्मानृशंस्याभ्यां न क्षान्त्या नार्जवेन च ।\nपुरुषः श्रियमाप्नोति न घृणित्वेन कर्हिचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In this world a man does not win prosperity by dharma, kindness, patience or straightforwardness, nor ever by tenderness.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"त्वां चेद्व्यसनमभ्यागादिदं भारत दुःसहम् ।\nयत्त्वं नार्हसि नापीमे भ्रातरस्ते महौजसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If this unbearable calamity has come upon you, Bharata, when you do not deserve it, nor do your mighty brothers,\""}},{"n":4,"text":"न हि तेऽध्यगमञ्जातु तदानीं नाद्य भारत ।\nधर्मात्प्रियतरं किंचिदपि चेज्जीवितादिह ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"then, Bharata, nothing, not even life itself, has ever seemed dearer to you than dharma, either then or now.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"धर्मार्थमेव ते राज्यं धर्मार्थं जीवितं च ते ।\nब्राह्मणा गुरवश्चैव जानन्त्यपि च देवताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Your kingdom is for dharma's sake and your life is for dharma's sake; the brahmins, the elders and even the gods know it.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"भीमसेनार्जुनौ चैव माद्रेयौ च मया सह ।\nत्यजेस्त्वमिति मे बुद्धिर्न तु धर्मं परित्यजेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I think you would give up Bhimasena, Arjuna, the sons of Madri and me, but you would never give up dharma.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"राजानं धर्मगोप्तारं धर्मो रक्षति रक्षितः ।\nइति मे श्रुतमार्याणां त्वां तु मन्ये न रक्षति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I have heard from the noble that dharma protects the king who guards dharma; but I think it does not protect you.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"अनन्या हि नरव्याघ्र नित्यदा धर्ममेव ते ।\nबुद्धिः सततमन्वेति छायेव पुरुषं निजा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"O tiger among men, your mind follows dharma alone, always, like one's own shadow follows a man.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"नावमंस्था हि सदृशान्नावराञ्श्रेयसः कुतः ।\nअवाप्य पृथिवीं कृत्स्नां न ते शृङ्गमवर्धत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You never scorned your equals, nor your inferiors, much less your betters; and even after winning the whole earth, your pride did not swell.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"स्वाहाकारैः स्वधाभिश्च पूजाभिरपि च द्विजान् ।\nदैवतानि पितॄंश्चैव सततं पार्थ सेवसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"With offerings of svaha and svadha and with worship, Partha, you constantly serve brahmins, gods and ancestors.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"ब्राह्मणाः सर्वकामैस्ते सततं पार्थ तर्पिताः ।\nयतयो मोक्षिणश्चैव गृहस्थाश्चैव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Brahmins, ascetics seeking liberation, and householders were always satisfied by you with all they desired, Partha.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"आरण्यकेभ्यो लौहानि भाजनानि प्रयच्छसि ।\nनादेयं ब्राह्मणेभ्यस्ते गृहे किंचन विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You give iron vessels to the forest hermits; there is nothing in your house that you would not give to brahmins.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"यदिदं वैश्वदेवान्ते सायंप्रातः प्रदीयते ।\nतद्दत्त्वातिथिभृत्येभ्यो राजञ्शेषेण जीवसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"After the Vaishvadeva offering, what is given morning and evening to guests and servants, king, you live on what remains.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"इष्टयः पशुबन्धाश्च काम्यनैमित्तिकाश्च ये ।\nवर्तन्ते पाकयज्ञाश्च यज्ञकर्म च नित्यदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Your sacrifices, the animal-bound rites, the rites for desired ends and occasional ones, the cooked-food offerings and all sacrificial work went on always.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"अस्मिन्नपि महारण्ये विजने दस्युसेविते ।\nराष्ट्रादपेत्य वसतो धार्मस्ते नावसीदति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Even in this great, lonely forest frequented by bandits, living away from your kingdom, your dharma does not fail.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"अश्वमेधो राजसूयः पुण्डरीकोऽथ गोसवः ।\nएतैरपि महायज्ञैरिष्टं ते भूरिदक्षिणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Ashvamedha, Rajasuya, Pundarika and Gosava sacrifices have all been performed by you with abundant gifts.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"राजन्परीतया बुद्ध्या विषमेऽक्षपराजये ।\nराज्यं वसून्यायुधानि भ्रातॄन्मां चासि निर्जितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"O king, with your mind overwhelmed, you were defeated at dice by foul play and lost your kingdom, wealth, weapons, brothers and me.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"ऋजोर्मृदोर्वदान्यस्य ह्रीमतः सत्यवादिनः ।\nकथमक्षव्यसनजा बुद्धिरापतिता तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How did a mind drawn to gambling come to you, so straightforward, gentle, generous, modest and truthful?\""}},{"n":19,"text":"अतीव मोहमायाति मनश्च परिदूयते ।\nनिशाम्य ते दुःखमिदमिमां चापदमीदृशीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"My mind is greatly bewildered and tormented, seeing this sorrow of yours and such a calamity.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"अत्राप्युदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nईश्वरस्य वशे लोकस्तिष्ठते नात्मनो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"On this point they recount an old tale: the world is in the power of the Lord and not under its own.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"धातैव खलु भूतानां सुखदुःखे प्रियाप्रिये ।\nदधाति सर्वमीशानः पुरस्ताच्छुक्रमुच्चरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Ordainer, the Lord, assigns to beings pleasure and pain, the dear and the unpleasant, appearing first to shape all.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"यथा दारुमयी योषा नरवीर समाहिता ।\nईरयत्यङ्गमङ्गानि तथा राजन्निमाः प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As a wooden puppet, hero among men, is made to move its limbs by one who sets it up, so, king, do these creatures move.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"आकाश इव भूतानि व्याप्य सर्वाणि भारत ।\nईश्वरो विदधातीह कल्याणं यच्च पापकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Lord, pervading all beings like space, ordains here what is good and what is evil.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"शकुनिस्तन्तुबद्धो वा नियतोऽयमनीश्वरः ।\nईश्वरस्य वशे तिष्ठन्नान्येषां नात्मनः प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This creature is like a bird tied with a string, controlled and not master of itself; it stays in the Lord's power, master neither of others nor of itself.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"मणिः सूत्र इव प्रोतो नस्योत इव गोवृषः ।\nधातुरादेशमन्वेति तन्मयो हि तदर्पणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Like a jewel strung on a thread, like a bull threaded through the nose, it follows the Ordainer's command, being made of him and offered to him.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"नात्माधीनो मनुष्योऽयं कालं भवति कंचन ।\nस्रोतसो मध्यमापन्नः कूलाद्वृक्ष इव च्युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Man is never his own master for any time, like a tree fallen from the bank into the middle of the stream.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"अज्ञो जन्तुरनीशोऽयमात्मनः सुखदुःखयोः ।\nईश्वरप्रेरितो गच्छेत्स्वर्गं नरकमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This ignorant creature is not master of its own pleasure and pain; urged by the Lord it goes to heaven or to hell.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"यथा वायोस्तृणाग्राणि वशं यान्ति बलीयसः ।\nधातुरेवं वशं यान्ति सर्वभूतानि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As the tips of grass fall under the power of a strong wind, so all beings, Bharata, come under the Ordainer's power.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"आर्यकर्मणि युञ्जानः पापे वा पुनरीश्वरः ।\nव्याप्य भूतानि चरते न चायमिति लक्ष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Lord, urging beings to noble deeds or to sin, moves pervading them, and is not seen.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"हेतुमात्रमिदं धातुः शरीरं क्षेत्रसंज्ञितम् ।\nयेन कारयते कर्म शुभाशुभफलं विभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This body, called the field, is a mere instrument of the Ordainer, by which the all-pervading one makes beings do deeds with good or bad fruit.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"पश्य मायाप्रभावोऽयमीश्वरेण यथा कृतः ।\nयो हन्ति भूतैर्भूतानि मोहयित्वात्ममायया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"See the power of the Lord's illusion: by deluding beings with his own magic, he makes beings kill beings.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"अन्यथा परिदृष्टानि मुनिभिर्वेददर्शिभिः ।\nअन्यथा परिवर्तन्ते वेगा इव नभस्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The sages who see the Veda have seen things in one way, and they turn out another way, like the gusts of the wind.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"अन्यथैव हि मन्यन्ते पुरुषास्तानि तानि च ।\nअन्यथैव प्रभुस्तानि करोति विकरोति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"People think these things in one way, but the Lord makes and unmakes them in another.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"यथा काष्ठेन वा काष्ठमश्मानं चाश्मना पुनः ।\nअयसा चाप्ययश्छिन्द्यान्निर्विचेष्टमचेतनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Just as one may cut wood with wood, stone with stone, and iron with iron, a thing without effort or consciousness,\""}},{"n":35,"text":"एवं स भगवान्देवः स्वयम्भूः प्रपितामहः ।\nहिनस्ति भूतैर्भूतानि छद्म कृत्वा युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"so, Yudhishthira, that blessed god, the self-born great-grandfather, uses disguise and destroys beings by beings.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"संप्रयोज्य वियोज्यायं कामकारकरः प्रभुः ।\nक्रीडते भगवान्भूतैर्बालः क्रीडनकैरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Joining and parting beings at his own will, the Lord plays with creatures as a child plays with toys.\""}},{"n":37,"text":"न मातृपितृवद्राजन्धाता भूतेषु वर्तते ।\nरोषादिव प्रवृत्तोऽयं यथायमितरो जनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Ordainer does not behave toward beings like a mother or father, O king; he acts as if in anger, like any other person.\""}},{"n":38,"text":"आर्याञ्शीलवतो दृष्ट्वा ह्रीमतो वृत्तिकर्शितान् ।\nअनार्यान्सुखिनश्चैव विह्वलामीव चिन्तया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Seeing the noble and virtuous, the modest, worn down by want, and the ignoble prospering, I am as if distraught with worry.\""}},{"n":39,"text":"तवेमामापदं दृष्ट्वा समृद्धिं च सुयोधने ।\nधातारं गर्हये पार्थ विषमं योऽनुपश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Seeing this calamity of yours and the prosperity of Suyodhana, Partha, I blame the Ordainer, who looks on so unequally.\""}},{"n":40,"text":"आर्यशास्त्रातिगे क्रूरे लुब्धे धर्मापचायिनि ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रे श्रियं दत्त्वा धाता किं फलमश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having given wealth to Dhritarashtra's son, cruel, greedy, transgressing the noble teachings and ruining dharma, what fruit does the Ordainer reap?\""}},{"n":41,"text":"कर्म चेत्कृतमन्वेति कर्तारं नान्यमृच्छति ।\nकर्मणा तेन पापेन लिप्यते नूनमीश्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If a deed follows the doer and reaches no other, then surely the Lord is stained by that sinful deed.\""}},{"n":42,"text":"अथ कर्म कृतं पापं न चेत्कर्तारमृच्छति ।\nकारणं बलमेवेह जनाञ्शोचामि दुर्बलान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"But if a sinful deed done does not reach the doer, then power alone is the cause here, and I grieve for the weak.\""}}]}]}